    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "urgent help needed. our reefer unit on the shipment from Hokkaido just flagged a temp spike. it's currently sitting at 8c and the sensors show it's rising. we have about 400kg of premium fatty tuna in there. what are the immediate steps we should take to minimize spoilage and what's the protocol for checking if the batch is still safe to sell?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Immediately deploy external cooling units near the reefer unit to help bring the temperature down as quickly as possible. Contact the carrier and logistics manager right away to initiate emergency temperature monitoring and potentially arrange for transfer to a functional cold storage area. For safety protocol, monitor the internal temperature constantly and arrange for expedited microbiological testing of the tuna by a certified lab. Do not proceed with selling the product until the lab confirms it meets all food safety standards.",
